\pi-0.225,l0.3,t0.3;1.^IALL WATER, RECLAIMED WATER AND SANITARY WASTEWATER WORK SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE LATEST JEA STANDARDS MANUAL, ALL APPLICABLE LOCAL AND STATE RULES AND REGULATIONS AND OTHER APPLICABLE JEA RULES.\P\P2.^IALL WAT
  3
ER, RECLAIMED WATER AND SANITARY WASTEWATER CONSTRUCTION SHALL BE PROVIDED BY A CONTRACTOR QUALIFIED AS REQUIRED UNDER THE CURRENT FLORIDA STATUTES OR BY AN UNDERGROUND UTILITY CONTRACTOR, LICENSED UNDER THE PROVISIONS OF CHAPTER 489 FS.\P\P3.^ITHE AP
  3
PLICANT SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR OBTAINING CITY, COUNTY OR FDOT ROW PERMITS FOR WORK IN THE CITY, COUNTY OR FDOT RIGHTS-OF-WAY.\P\P4.^ITHE APPLICANT SHALL CONTACT JEA AND SCHEDULE A PRE-CONSTRUCTION MEETING TO BE HELD PRIOR TO INITIATING THE JEA WATER
  3
 AND WASTEWATER UTILITY WORK, INCLUDING ALL UTILITY MAIN TAPS BY THE CONTRACTOR.\P\P5.^IJEA WATER AND WASTEWATER TAP FEES, CAPACITY FEES AND METER FEES SHALL BE PAID PRIOR TO THE WATER METER INSTALLATION. WATER METERS WILL NOT BE INSTALLED PRIOR TO IS
  3
SUANCE OF REQUIRED ACCEPTANCE (TRANSFER OF OWNERSHIP) DOCUMENTS WHICH MAY INCLUDE THE ISSUANCE OF A REGULATORY CLEARANCE LETTER (COC) FOR THE WATER AND WASTEWATER IMPROVEMENTS, COMPLETION AND APPROVAL OF FINAL INSPECTION AND AS-BUILT DRAWINGS.\P\P6.^I
  3
FINAL CONNECTION TO THE JEA SYSTEM MAY BE CONTINGENT UPON THE CONSTRUCTION, DEDICATION AND FINAL ACCEPTANCE OF THE JEA OFF-SITE UTILITIES.\P\P7.^IMINIMUM HORIZONTAL AND VERTICAL SEPARATIONS FOR WATER, RECLAIMED WATER AND WASTEWATER IMPROVEMENTS SHALL 
  3
CONFORM TO THE LATEST JEA AND FDEP RULES. THE MINIMUM HORIZONTAL SEPARATION BETWEEN THE PROPOSED WATER AND WASTEWATER UTILITIES AND PONDS OR STRUCTURES SHALL CONFORM TO THE LATEST JEA WATER AND WASTEWATER STANDARDS MANUAL.\P\P8.^IWATER AND WASTEWATER 
  3
PIPES LESS THAN 24" IN DIAMETER SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED WITH A MINIMUM 30" COVER IN UNPAVED OR SIDEWALK AREAS AND A MINIMUM OF 36" COVER IN PAVED AREAS. THE MAXIMUM COVER FOR UTILITIES, BOTH OPEN CUT AND UTILIZING HDD METHODS SHALL COMPLY WITH THE LATES
  3
T JEA WATER AND WASTEWATER STANDARDS MANUAL.\P\P9.^IWATER AND WASTEWATER PRESSURE MAINS AND SERVICES SHALL PASS A JEA PRESSURE AND LEAKAGE TEST AT 150-PSI MINIMUM OR TWO TIMES OPERATING PRESSURE, FOR 2-HOURS. IN ADDITION, WATER MAINS SHALL BE DISINFEC
  3
TED AND PASS A BACTERIOLOGICAL ANALYSIS. ALL TESTS SHALL CONFORM TO JEA AND FDEP RULES, REGULATIONS AND AWWA C-651. THE JEA INSPECTOR SHALL BE NOTIFIED 72-HOURS (MIN) PRIOR TO PERFORMING THESE TESTS. NO FINAL CONNECTION(S) TO EXISTING POTABLE WATER M
  3
AINS SHALL BE MADE UNTIL THE NEW MAIN IS PRESSURE TESTED, DISINFECTED AND CLEARED FOR SERVICE.\P\P10.^IIN THE AREAS WHERE SOLVENT CONTAMINATION IS FOUND IN THE TRENCH, WORK SHALL BE STOPPED AND THE PROPER REGULATORY AUTHORITIES NOTIFIED. A REVISED CON
  3
STRUCTION PLAN SHALL BE APPROVED BY JEA AND FDEP THAT COMPLIES WITH ALL REGULATORY RULES. THE REVISED CONSTRUCTION PLAN FOR THE JEA WATER MAIN SYSTEM INCLUDING WATER SERVICE LINES MAY INVOLVE GALVANIZED OR DUCTILE IRON PIPE WITH SPECIAL SOLVENT RESIS
  3
TANT (FLUOROCARBON TYPE) GASKETS THAT EXTEND 100' BEYOND THE CONTAMINATED AREAS.\P\P11.^ITHE CONTRACTOR SHALL MINIMIZE SERVICE INTERRUPTIONS TO EXISTING JEA WATER AND WASTEWATER CUSTOMERS. IF JEA APPROVES A SERVICE INTERRUPTION, THEN THE CONTRACTOR WI
  3
LL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR NOTIFYING THE AFFECTED CUSTOMERS IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE LATEST JEA RULES.\P\P12.^IRESIDENTIAL SERVICES USING RECLAIMED WATER FOR IRRIGATION MUST HAVE A JEA APPROVED BACKFLOW PREVENTER INSTALLED ON EACH POTABLE WATER SERVICE PRIOR
  3
 TO THE INSTALLATION OF A JEA RECLAIMED WATER METER. THE INSTALLATION OF A BACKFLOW PREVENTER SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE JEA RULES AND REGULATIONS FOR WATER, SEWER AND RECLAIMED WATER SERVICES, APPENDIX B, CROSS CONNECTION CONTROL POLICY.\P\P13.
  3
^IFOR DEVELOPMENTS UTILIZING RECLAIMED WATER, A JEA APPROVED RECLAIMED WATER SIGNAGE PLAN SHALL BE IMPLEMENTED PRIOR TO THE INSTALLATION OF THE RECLAIMED WATER METERS.\P\P14.^IALL BACKFLOW PREVENTERS SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH JEA CROSS CONNECTION PRO
  1
GRAM. BACKFLOW PREVENTERS MUST BE TESTED AFTER INSTALLATION BY A CERTIFIED TESTER AND ANNUALLY THEREAFTER. JEA CONTACT: PERMITTING 904-665-7988\P\P15.^IBACKFLOW PREVENTERS ON FIRE LINES OR COMBINATION FIRE/POTABLE MAINS SHALL HAVE FREEZE PROTECTION.
  7
