{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;Annual reports in compliance with the SJRWMD stormwater permits are required from the maintenance entity of all stormwater management facilities. Send copies of the reports to:\P\H0.625x;\PEngineering and Construction Management
  3
\PEdward Ball Building, 10th Floor\P214 N. Hogan St.\PJacksonville, FL 32202\Phttp://www.coj.net/Departments/Public+Works/Engineering+and+Construction+Management/\P\P\H1.6x;The owner of any project one (1) acre or larger is required to provide a Noti
  3
ce of Intent (NOI) in accordance with criteria set forth in the city’s NPDES permit within 48 hours of beginning construction. Send NOI and NOI fee to:\P\H0.625x;\PFlorida Department of Environmental Protection\PNPDES Stormwater Notices Center, Mail 
  3
Station #2510\P2600 Blair Stone Road\PTallahassee, Florida 32399-2400\P(866) 336-6312\Phttp://www.dep.state.fl.us/water/stormwater/npdes/\P\P\H1.6x;The contractor shall contact the Environmental Quality Division, Erosion and Sedimentation Control Sec
  3
tion (ESC) to provide verification that applicable stormwater permits have been obtained and to schedule a pre-construction ESC site inspection:\P\H0.625x;\PEnvironmental Quality Division\P407 North Laura Street, Third Floor\PJacksonville, FL, 32202\
  1
P(904) 255-7222}
