{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;CITY: Except for new subdivision infrastructure construction, all work performed within a City of Jacksonville right-of-way or easement requires a Right-of-way Permit. The contractor performing the proposed work must have a curr
  3
ent Right-of-way Bond on file with Development Services. Right-of-way Permit applications are processed at:\P\H0.625x;\PDevelopment Services Customer Service Counter\PEdward Ball Building, 2nd Floor\P214 N. Hogan St.\PJacksonville, FL 32202\P(904) 25
  3
5-8572\Phttp://row.jaxdev.info/\P\P\H1.6x;STATE: All work performed within a state right-of-way requires a permit from the Florida Department of Transportation (FDOT). It is the developer’s responsibility to obtain required FDOT permits or maintenanc
  3
e-of-traffic approvals for work within FDOT right-of-ways. The FDOT regional office can be contacted at (904) 360-5200 Any changes to the approved plans needed for FDOT approval must be submitted to Development Services as revisions.\P\PAdjacent Stat
  3
e Roads:  ______________________________________________________________________\P\PRAILROAD: Railroad companies may require special approvals or permits to work within their right-of-ways. It is the developer’s responsibility to obtain permission fr
  1
om any railroad right-of-way owner before performing any work within their right-of-way.}
