            MAINTENANCE/INSPECTION PROCEDURES\P\P\PEROSION AND SEDIMENT CONTROL INSPECTION AND MAINTENANCE \PPRACTICES\P\PTHE FOLLOWING ARE INSPECTION AND MAINTENANCE PRACTICES THAT \PWILL BE USED TO MAINTAIN EROSION AND SEDIMENT CONTROLS.\P\P1. NO M
  3
ORE THAN 10 ACRES OF THE SITE WILL BE DENUDED AT ONE \P   TIME WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM THE ENGINEER.  \P\P2. ALL CONTROL MEASURES WILL BE INSPECTED BY THE  \P   SUPERINTENDENT, THE PERSON RESPONSIBLE FOR THE DAY TO\P   DAY SITE OPERATION OR S
  3
OMEONE APPOINTED BY THE \P   SUPERINTENDENT, AT LEAST ONCE A WEEK AND FOLLOWING ANY\P   STORM EVENT OF 0.25 INCHES OR GREATER. \P\P3. ALL TURBIDITY CONTROL MEASURES WILL BE MAINTAINED IN GOOD \P   WORKING ORDER; IF A REPAIR IS NECESSARY, IT WILL BE I
  3
NITIATED\P   WITHIN 24 HOURS OF REPORT.\P\P4. BUILT UP SEDIMENT WILL BE REMOVED FROM SILT FENCE WHEN IT \P   HAS REACHED ONE-THIRD THE HEIGHT OF THE FENCE.\P\P5. SILT FENCE WILL BE INSPECTED FOR DEPTH  OF SEDIMENT, TEARS,\P   TO SEE IF THE FABRIC IS 
  3
SECURELY ATTACHED TO THE FENCE POSTS,\P   AND TO SEE THAT THE FENCE POSTS ARE FIRMLY IN THE GROUND.\P\P6. THE SEDIMENT BASINS WILL BE INSPECTED FOR THE DEPTH OF\P   SEDIMENT, AND BUILT UP SEDIMENT WILL BE REMOVED WHEN IT \P   REACHES 10 PERCENT OF TH
  3
E DESIGN CAPACITY OR AT THE END OF \P   THE JOB.\P\P7. DIVERSION DIKES/SWALES WILL BE INSPECTED AND ANY BREACHES \P   PROMPTLY REPAIRED.\P\P8. TEMPORARY AND PERMANENT SEEDING AND PLANTING WILL BE\P   INSPECTED FOR BARE SPOTS, WASHOUTS, AND HEALTHY GR
  3
OWTH.\P\P9. A MAINTENANCE INSPECTION REPORT WILL BE MADE AFTER EACH \P   INSPECTION. A COPY OF THE REPORT FORM TO BE COMPLETED BY \P   THE INSPECTOR IS ATTACHED.\P   THE REPORTS WILL BE KEPT ON SITE DURING CONSTRUCTION AND \P   AVAILABLE UPON REQUEST
  3
 TO THE OWNER, ENGINEER, OR ANY  \P   FEDERAL, STATE, OR LOCAL AGENCY APPROVING SEDIMENT AND \P   EROSION PLANS, OR STORM WATER MANAGEMENT PLANS.\P   THE REPORTS SHALL BE MADE AND RETAINED AS PART OF THE \P   STORM WATER POLLUTION PREVENTION PLAN FOR
  3
 AT LEAST THREE\P   YEARS FROM THE DATE THAT THE SITE IS FINALLY STABILIZED AND\P   THE NOTICE TERMINATION IS SUBMITTED. THE REPORTS SHALL \P   IDENTIFY ANY INCIDENTS OF NON- COMPLIANCE.\P\P10. THE SITE SUPERINTENDENT WILL SELECT UP TO THREE INDIVIDU
  3
ALS\P    WHO WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR INSPECTIONS, MAINTENANCE, AND\P    REPAIR ACTIVITIES, AND FILLING OUT THE INSPECTION AND \P    MAINTENANCE REPORT.\P\P11. PERSONNEL SELECTED FOR INSPECTION AND MAINTENANCE\P    RESPONSIBILITIES WILL RECEIVE TRAINI
  3
NG FROM THE SITE\P    SUPERINTENDENT. THEY WILL BE TRAINED IN ALL THE INSPECTION\P    AND MAINTENANCE PRACTICES NECESSARY FOR KEEPING THE \P    EROSION AND SEDIMENT CONTROLS USED ONSITE IN GOOD \P    WORKING ORDER.\P\PNON-STORM WATER DISCHARGES\P\P1.
  3
 IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE FOLLOWING NON-STORM WATER \P   DISCHARGES WILL OCCUR FROM THE SITE DURING THE \P   CONSTRUCTION PERIOD:\P\P2. WATER FROM WATER LINE FLUSHING\P\P3. PAVEMENT WASH WATERS ( WHERE NO SPILLS OR LEAKS OF TOXIC\P   OR HAZARDOUS MATE
  3
RIALS HAVE OCCURRED). \P\P4. UNCONTAMINATED GROUNDWATER (FROM DEWATERING  \P   EXCAVATION).\P\PALL NON-STORM WATER DISCHARGES WILL BE DIRECTED TO THE \PSEDIMENT BASIN PRIOR TO DISCHARGE.\P\P\PCONTRACTOR'S CERTIFICATION\P\PI CERTIFY UNDER PENALTY OF L
  3
AW THAT I UNDERSTAND THE TERMS \PAND CONDITIONS OF THE GENERAL NATIONAL POLLUTANT DISCHARGE \PELIMINATION SYSTEM (NPDES) PERMIT THAT AUTHORIZES THE STORM \PWATER DISCHARGES ASSOCIATED WITH INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITY FROM THE \PCONSTRUCTION SITE IDENTIFIED A
  1
S PART OF THIS CERTIFICATION.
  7
