                   PRODUCT SPECIFIC PRACTICES\PTHE FOLLOWING PRODUCT SPECIFIC PRACTICES WILL BE FOLLOWED \PONSITE:\P\PPETROLEUM PRODUCTS\P   \PALL ONSITE VEHICLES WILL BE MONITORED FOR LEAKS AND \PRECEIVE REGULAR PREVENTIVE  MAINTENANCE TO REDUCE THE
  3
 \PCHANCE OF LEAKAGE. PETROLEUM PRODUCTS WILL BE STORED \PIN TIGHTLY SEALED CONTAINERS WHICH ARE CLEARLY LABELED. \PANY ASPHALT SUBSTANCES USED ONSITE WILL BE APPLIED \PACCORDING TO THE MANUFACTURERS RECOMMENDATIONS.\P\PFERTILIZERS\P\PFERTILIZERS USE
  3
D WILL APPLIED ONLY IN THE MINIMUM \PAMOUNTS RECOMMENDED BY THE MANUFACTURER. ONCE \PAPPLIED, FERTILIZER WILL BE WORKED INTO THE SOIL TO LIMIT \PEXPOSURE TO STORM WATER. STORAGE WILL BE IN A COVERED \PAREA. THE CONTENTS OF ANY PARTIALLY USED BAGS OF 
  3
\PFERTILIZER WILL BE TRANSFERRED TO A SEALABLE  PLASTIC BIN \PTO AVOID SPILLS.\P\PPAINTS\P\PALL CONTAINERS WILL BE TIGHTLY SEALED AND STORED WHEN \PNOT REQUIRED FOR USE. EXCESS PAINT WILL NOT BE \PDISCHARGED TO THE STORM SEWER SYSTEM BUT WILL BE \PPR
  1
OPERLY DISPOSED OF ACCORDING TO MANUFACTURERS' \PINSTRUCTIONS OR STATE AND LOCAL REGULATIONS. \P\PCONCRETE TRUCKS\P\PCONCRETE TRUCKS WILL NOT BE ALLOWED TO WASH OUT OR \PDISCHARGE SURPLUS CONCRETE OR DRUM WASH WATER ON THE \PSITE.
  7
