                               SPILL PREVENTION\P\P\PMATERIAL MANAGEMENT PRACTICES\P\PTHE FOLLOWING ARE THE MATERIAL MANAGEMENT PRACTICES THAT \PWILL BE USED TO REDUCE THE RISK OF SPILLS OR OTHER ACCIDENTAL \PEXPOSURE OF MATERIALS AND SUBSTANCES TO S
  3
TORM WATER RUNOFF.\P\P\PGOOD HOUSEKEEPING\P\PTHE FOLLOWING GOOD HOUSEKEEPING PRACTICES WILL BE FOLLOWED \PONSITE DURING THE CONSTRUCTION PROJECT.\P\P1. AN EFFORT WILL BE MADE TO STORE ONLY ENOUGH PRODUCT \P   REQUIRED TO DO THE JOB.\P\P2. ALL MATERIA
  3
LS STORED ONSITE WILL BE STORED IN A NEAT, ORDERLY \P   MANNER IN THEIR APPROPRIATE CONTAINERS AND, IF POSSIBLE, UNDER A \P   ROOF OR OTHER ENCLOSURE.\P\P3. PRODUCTS WILL BE KEPT IN THEIR ORIGINAL CONTAINERS WITH THE \P   ORIGINAL MANUFACTURERS LABEL
  3
.\P\P4. SUBSTANCES WILL NOT BE MIXED WITH ONE ANOTHER UNLESS \P   RECOMMENDED BY THE MANUFACTURER. \P\P5. WHENEVER POSSIBLE, ALL OF A PRODUCT WILL BE USED UP BEFORE \P   DISPOSING OF THE CONTAINER.  \P \P6. MANUFACTURER'S RECOMMENDATIONS FOR PROPER U
  3
SE AND \P   DISPOSAL WILL BE FOLLOWED. \P\P7. THE SITE SUPERINTENDENT WILL INSPECT DAILY TO ENSURE \P   MATERIALS ONSITE RECEIVE PROPER USE AND DISPOSAL. \P\P\PHAZARDOUS PRODUCTS\P\P\PTHESE PRACTICES ARE USED TO REDUCE THE RISKS ASSOCIATED WITH \PHAZ
  3
ARDOUS MATERIALS.\P\P1. PRODUCTS WILL BE KEPT IN ORIGINAL CONTAINERS UNLESS THEY ARE \P   NOT RESEALABLE.    \P\P2. ORIGINAL LABELS AND MATERIAL SAFETY DATA WILL BE RETAINED; \P   THEY CONTAIN IMPORTANT PRODUCT INFORMATION.  \P\P3. IF SURPLUS PRODUCT
  1
 MUST BE DISPOSED OF, MANUFACTURER'S OR \P   LOCAL AND STATE RECOMMENDED METHODS FOR PROPER DISPOSAL \P   WILL BE FOLLOWED.    
  7
