\PSTRUCTURAL PRACTICES\P\P1.    TEMPORARY DIVERSION DIKE: TEMPORARY DIVERSION DIKES MAY \P      BE USED TO DIVERT RUNOFF TROUGH A SEDIMENT-TRAPPING \P      FACILITY.\P   \P2.    TEMPORARY SEDIMENT TRAP: A SEDIMENT TRAP IS USUALLY \P      INSTALLED IN
  3
 A DRAINAGE WAY AT A STORM DRAIN INLET OR AT \P      OTHER POINTS OF DISCHARGE FROM A DISTURBED AREA WITH THE\P      FOLLOWING LIMITATIONS:\P       A. THE SEDIMENT TRAP MAY BE INSTRUCTED EITHER \P          INDEPENDENTLY OR IN CONJUNCTION WITH A TEMPO
  3
RARY   \P          DIVERSION DIKE.\P     \P3. OUTLET PROTECTION: APPLICABLE TO THE OUTLETS OF ALL PIPES\P   AND PAVED CHANNEL SECTIONS WHERE THE VELOCITY OF FLOW \P   AT DESIGN CAPACITY OF THE OUTLET WILL EXCEED THE \P   PERMISSIBLE VELOCITY OF THE R
  3
ECEIVING CHANNEL OR AREA.\P   \P4. SEDIMENT BASIN: WILL BE CONSTRUCTED AT THE COMMON \P   DRAINAGE LOCATIONS THAT SERVE AN AREA WITH 10 OR MORE\P   DISTURBED ACRES AT ONE TIME. THE PROPOSED STORM WATER \P   PONDS (OR TEMPORARY PONDS) WILL BE CONSTRUC
  3
TED FOR USE\P   AS SEDIMENT BASINS. THESE SEDIMENT BASINS MUST PROVIDE A\P   MINIMUM OF 3, 600 CUBIC FEET OF STORAGE PER ACRE DRAINED \P   UNTIL FINAL STABILIZATION OF THE SITE. THE 3, 600 CUBIC FEET\P   OF STORAGE AREA PER ACRE DRAINED DOES NOT APPL
  3
Y TO FLOWS \P   FROM OFFSITE AREAS AND FLOWS FROM ONSITE AREAS THAT ARE\P   EITHER UNDISTURBED OR HAVE UNDERGONE FINAL \P   STABILIZATION WHERE SUCH FLOWS ARE DIVERTED AROUND \P   BOTH THE DISTURBED AREA AND THE SEDIMENT BASIN. ANY\P   TEMPORARY SEDI
  1
MENT BASINS CONSTRUCTED MUST BE \P   BACKFILLED AND COMPACTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE \P   SPECIFICATIONS  FOR STRUCTURAL FILL. ALL SEDIMENT\P   COLLECTED IN PERMANENT OR TEMPORARY SEDIMENT TRAPS\P   MUST BE REMOVED UPON FINAL STABILIZATION.\P\P    
  7
