     5
  3
{\fArial|b1|i0|c0|p34;\H1.5x;\LPUMP}\PPUMP SHALL BE OF THE CENTRIFUGAL TYPE WITH AN INTEGRALLY BUILT-IN GRINDER UNIT AND SUBMERSIBLE TYPE MOTOR.  DISCHARGE SHALL BE 1-1/4" NPT.  THE PUMP VOLUTE, MOTOR AND SEAL HOUSING SHALL BE HIGH QUALITY GRAY CAST 
  3
IRON, ASTM A-48, CLASS 30.  ALL EXTERNAL MATING PARTS SHALL BE MACHINED AND NITRILE O-RING SEALED ON A BEVELED EDGE.  GASKETS SHALL NOT BE ACCEPTABLE.  ALL FASTENERS EXPOSED TO THE PUMPED LIQUID SHALL BE 300 SERIES STAINLESS STEEL.\P\P{\fArial|b1|i0|
  3
c0|p34;\LPOWER CORD }- POWER CORD SHALL BE SJOOW WATER RESISTANT 300V, UL APPROVED.  THE CABLE JACKET SHALL BE SEALED AT THE MOTOR ENTRANCE BY MEANS OF A RUBBER COMPRESSION WASHER AND COMPRESSION NUT.  A HEAT SHRINK TUBE FILLED WITH EPOXY SHALL SEAL 
  3
THE OUTER CABLE JACKET AND THE INDIVIDUAL LEADS TO PREVENT WATER FROM ENTERING THE MOTOR. \P\P{\fArial|b1|i0|c0|p34;\LMOTOR\l -}  PUMP MOTOR SHALL BE RATED 2 HP AT 3450 RPM.  MOTOR SHALL BE FOR 60HZ, SINGLE-PHASE, 230 VOLTS. MOTOR SHALL BE CAPACITOR 
  3
START, CAPACITOR RUN-TYPE FOR HIGH STARTING TORQUE.  THE STATOR, ROTOR AND BEARINGS SHALL BE MOUNTED IN A SEALED SUBMERSIBLE-TYPE HOUSING.  THE STATOR WINDINGS SHALL HAVE CLASS F INSULATION (155°C OR 311°F) AND A DIELECTRIC OIL-FILLED MOTORS, NEMA L 
  3
DESIGN (SINGLE-PHASE).  BECAUSE AIR-FILLED MOTORS DO NOT DISSIPATE THE AS EFFICIENTLY AS OIL-FILLED MOTOR, THEY SHALL NOT BE ACCEPTABLE.  THE PUMP AND MOTOR SHALL BE SPECIFICALLY DESIGNED SO THAT THEY MAY BE OPERATED PARTIALLY DRY AND COMPLETELY SUBM
  3
ERGED IN THE LIQUID BEING PUMPED.  THE PUMP SHALL NOT BE REQUIRE COOLING WATER JACKETS.  SUPPLEMENTAL COOLING SHALL NOT BE ACCEPTABLE.\P\PTHE MOTOR SHALL HAVE A CURRENT OVERLOAD ATTACHED TO THE TOP END OF THE MOTOR WINDINGS TO STOP THE MOTOR IF THE M
  3
OTOR WINDING TEMPERATURE REACHES 138°C.  THE HIGH TEMPERATURE SHUT-OFF WILL CAUSE THE PUMP TO CEASE OPERATION, SHOULD A CONTROL FAILURE CAUSE THE PUMP TO RUN IN A DRY WET WELL.  THE THERMOSTAT SHALL RESET AUTOMATICALLY WHEN THE MOTOR COOLS TO A SAFE 
  3
OPERATING TEMPERATURE.\P\P{\fArial|b1|i0|c0|p34;\LBEARINGS AND SHAFT}- AN UPPER SINGLE-ROW BALL RADIAL BEARING AND A LOWER SINGLE-ROW BALL THRUST BEARING SHALL BE PROVIDED.  BEARING SHALL BE PERMANENTLY LUBRICATED BY THE DIELECTRIC OIL THAT FILL THE 
  3
MOTOR HOUSING.  THE SHAFT SHALL BE MACHINED FROM SOLID 416 SERIES STAINLESS STEEL AND BE DESIGNED WITH LARGE DIAMETERS AND MINIMUM OVERHANG TO REDUCE SHAFT DEFLECTION AND PROLONG BEARING AND SEAL LIFE.\P\P{\fArial|b1|i0|c0|p34;\LSEALS-}  THE ROTOR AN
  3
D STATOR IN THE MOTOR HOUSING SHALL BE SEPARATED AND PROTECTED FROM THE PUMPED LIQUID BY AN OIL-FILLED SEAL HOUSING INCORPORATING A TYPE 21 CARBON CERAMIC MECHANICAL SEAL.\P\P{\fArial|b1|i0|c0|p34;\LIMPELLER}- THE IMPELLER SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED OF 316
  3
/CF8M STAINLESS STEEL AND BE DESIGNED FOR ROUGH DUTY SERVICE.  IT SHALL BE A TEN-VANE, SEMI-OPEN DESIGN WITH FOUR WASH OUT VANES ON THE REAR SHROUD.  THE IMPELLER SHALL BE A NON-OVERLOADING DESIGN.\P\P{\fArial|b1|i0|c0|p34;\LGRINDER MECHANISM}- THE S
  3
TATIONARY CUTTER SHALL BE CIRCUILAR IN DESIGN AND CONTAIN EVENLY SPACED CUTTING SLOTS THAT EXTEND OUTWARD FROM THE INLET OF THE PUMP.  THE SLOTS ARE TAPERED INWARD TOWARD THE INLET TO HELP DIRECT SLURRY THROUGH THE CUTTING SLOTS INTO THE PUMP.  THE S
  3
LOTS ARE TO BE ANGLED, OR UNDERCUT, TO HELP AMINTAIN A SHAP AXIAL CUTTING EDGE, EVEN AS THE AXIAL FACE WEARS DRUING USE.  THE STATIONARY CUTTER SHALL BE PRESSED INTO THE SUCTION OPENING OF THE VOLUTE AND HELD IN PLACE BY FOUR 300 SERIES STAINLESS STE
  3
EL SCREWS.  THE STATIONAL CUTTER SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH  TAPPED BVACK-OFF HOLES SO THAT SCREWS CAN BE USED TO REMOVE THE CUTTER FROM THE VOLUTE.  THE ROTATING CUTTER SHALL CONTAIN THREE AXIAL CUTTING ARMS EXTENDING FROM THE  HUB, PERPENDICULAR TO THE
  3
 PUMP SHAFT, THAT ARE SHAPED TO AID IN THE REFECTION OF SUSPENDED DEBRIS THAT HAS NOT BEEN SUFFICIENTLY REDUCED IN SIZE BY THE AXIAL CUTTING ACTION.  THE CURVED, LEADING EDGE OF THE CUTTING ARMS SHALL CREATE A SCISSOR ACTION WITH THE CUTTING SLOTS OF
  3
 THE STATIONARY CUTTER PLATE TO MINIMIZE THE REQUIRED TORQUE.  THIS WILL ALLOW THE CUTTER TO MACERATE TOUGH OBJECTS AND PROLONG CUTTER LIFE.  SERRATIONS ON THE HUB OF THE CUTTER ADD ADDITINAL CUTS THAT PREVENT DEBRIS FROM BECOMING ENTANGELED WITHIN T
  3
HE ROTATING CUTTER.  THE ROTATING CUTTER SHALL THREAD ONTO THE END OF THE PUMP SHAFT AND BE SECURED BY A 300 SERIES STAINLESS STEEL WASHER IN CONJUNCTION WITH A 300 SERIES STAINLESS STEEL FLAT HEAD CAP SCREW THREADED INTO THE END OF THE SHAFT.  BOTH 
  3
STATIONARY AND ROTATING CUTTERS SHALL BE MADE OF 440C STAINLESS STEEL, HARDENED TO ROCKWELL 57-60C AND GROUND CLOSE TO TOLERANCE.  THE GRINDER SHALL BE CAPABLE OF GRINDER NORMAL DOMESTIC SEWAGE INTO A FINE SLURRY. \P\P{\fArial|b1|i0|c0|p34;\H1.5x;\LW
  3
ET WELL-\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;\l\P}WET WELL SHALL BE A FILAMENT WOUND FIBERGLASS BASIN USING A COMMERCIAL GRADE OF GLASS FIBER HAVING A COUPLING AGENT WHICH WILL PROVIDE A SUITABLE BOND BETWEEN THE GLASS REINFORCEMENT AND THE RESIN.  THE LAMINATE SHAL
  3
L CONSIST OF AN INNER SURFACE, AN INTERIOR LAYER, AND AN EXTERIOR LAYER OF LAMINATE BODY.  THE INNER SURFACE SHALL BE FREE OF CRACKS AND CRAZING WITH A SMOOTH FINISH.  SOME WAVINESS IS PERMISSIBLE AS LONG AS THE SURFACE IS SMOOTH AND FREE OF PITS.  B
  3
ETWEEN 0.010 AND 0.020 INCHES OF RESIN-RICH SURFACE SHALL BE PROVIDED.  THE BASIN SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH AN ANTI-FLOATATION RING TO PREVENT RISING. THE BASIN SHALL BE PLACED ON STABLE FOOTING WITH EITHER  57-STONE OR CONCRETE BASE.      \P\P{\fArial|
  3
b1|i0|c0|p34;\H1.5x;\LWET WELL COVER-}\PWET WELL LID COVER SHALL BE FABRICATED FROM 1/4" ALUMINUM DIAMOND PLATE OR 1/2" NON-SKID SOLID GREEN FIBERGLASS AND BUILT TO WITHSTAND A LOAD OF 150 LB. P.S.F. OR EQUAL. STAINLESS STEEL BOLTS, NUTS AND HINGES -
  3
 LOCKING STAPLE. \P\P{\H1.5x;\LFLOATS-}\PFLOATS SHALL BE ANCHOR SCIENTIFIC S30N0 ROTO-FLOATS OR EQUAL. \P\P{\H1.5x;\LACCESSORIES -}\P--STAINLESS STEEL CABLE RACK  \P-- STAINLESS STEEL LIFT CABLES\P\P {\fArial|b1|i0|c0|p34;\H1.5x;\LANTI-FLOATATION-} \
  1
PCONCRETE IS RECOMMENDED TO PREVENT FLOATATION OF THE FIBERGLASS BASIN.  THE FOLLOWING LISTS THE CUBIC FEET REQUIRED PER FOOT OF BASIN DEPTH.
  7
