\pi-0.14447,l0.14447,t0.01204,0.12039;{\LNOTES:}\P\P\pi-0.09631,l0.09631,t0.09631,0.12039;1.^ITRENCH SIDES SHALL BE APPROXIMATELY VERTICAL BETWEEN AN ELEVATION OF 1 FOOT ABOVE THE TOP OF THE PIPE AND THE \P\pi0,t0.01204,0.12039;CENTER LINE OF THE PIPE
  3
; OTHERWISE, TRENCH SIDES SHALL BE AS VERTICAL AS POSSIBLE OR AS REQUIRED BY OSHA \PSTANDARDS. REFER TO THE MEASUREMENT AND PAYMENT SECTION (SECTION #801, PARAGRAPH #4)) TO DETERMINE MAXIMUM \PPAYLINE WIDTHS.\P\pi-0.14447,l0.14447;\P\pi-0.09631,l0.09
  3
631,t0.09631,0.12039;2.^IBELL HOLE SHALL BE DUG TO PERMIT THE ENTIRE STRAIGHT BARREL OF THE PIPE TO REST ON THE UNDISTURBED TRENCH \P\pi0,t0.01204,0.12039;BOTTOM. BOULDERS OR LOOSE ROCKS LARGER THAN 3/4 INCH IN SIZE WILL NOT BE PERMITTED IN BACKFILL U
  3
P TO 1 FOOT \PABOVE THE TOP OF THE PIPE.\P\pi-0.14447,l0.14447;\P\pi-0.09631,l0.09631,t0.09631,0.12039;3.^IBACK FILL MATERIAL UP TO A LEVEL OF 1 FOOT OVER THE PIPE SHALL CONSIST OF AASHTO CLASS A-3 SOIL (SUITABLE SOIL) AND \P\pi0,t0.01204,0.12039;SHAL
  3
L EXCLUDE CLAY MATERIALS AND LOOSE ROCKS LARGER THAN 3/4 INCH SIZE.\P\pi-0.14447,l0.14447;\P\pi-0.09631,l0.09631,t0.09631,0.12039;4.^IBACKFILL MATERIAL UP TO A LEVEL 1 FOOT OVER THE TOP OF PIPE OR BOTTOM OF STRUCTURES SHALL BE PLACED IN 6 INCH \P\pi0,
  3
t0.01204,0.12039;COMPACTED THICKNESS LAYERS AND SHALL BE COMPACTED TO 98% OF IT'S MAXIMUM DENSITY AS DETERMINED BY THE \PLABORATORY MODIFIED PROCTOR TEST, ASTM D1557.\P\pi-0.14447,l0.14447;\P\pi-0.09631,l0.09631,t0.09631,0.12039;5.^ISEE " EXCAVATION A
  1
ND EARTHWORK", SECTION 408 FOR ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS INCLUDING REMOVAL AND REPLACEMENT \P\pi0,t0.01204,0.12039;OF UNSUITABLE SOILS, DEWATERING, COMPACTION REQUIREMENTS AND DENSITY TESTING OF COMPACTED SOILS.
