\pi-0.24,l0.32,t0.32;1)^ITHIS LOW PRESSURE (LP) SEWER SERVICE ARRANGEMENT IS FOR SPECIAL CASES ONLY AND MUST FIRST BE APPROVED BY JEA MANAGEMENT PRIOR TO DESIGN OR CONSTRUCTION. THIS LP SEWER MANIFOLD ARRANGEMENT MAY BE UTILIZED TO SERVE UP TO 9 EQUIV
  3
ALENT RESIDENTIAL UNITS (ERU) AND SHALL BE PERMITTED SIMILAR TO A GRAVITY SEWER MAIN. THIS STANDARD SHALL APPLY TO RESIDENTIAL CUSTOMERS ONLY.\P2)^IRESIDENTIAL PUMP STATION (PS) SHALL BE MAINTAINED BY THE CUSTOMER. EACH RESIDENT IS RESPONSIBLE FOR RET
  3
AINING THE SERVICE OF A COMPETENT MAINTENANCE ENTITY TO SERVE THEIR PRIVATE LP SYSTEM. THE CUSTOMER IS RESPONSIBLE FOR FINAL PUMP DESIGN AND SELECTION. A CHECK VALVE AND BALL VALVE SHALL BE PROVIDED AT THE PROPERTY LINE AND MAINTAINED BY THE CUSTOMER
  3
 (SEE DETAIL).\P3)^IEACH CUSTOMER SHALL HAVE A SEPARATE LP SERVICE CONNECTION POINT (SEE DETAIL). THIS BOX (2" METER BOX WITH PVC PLUG IN TOP) SHALL BE APPROXIMATELY 7 FEET INSIDE THE R/W AND A MINIMUM OF 6 FEET FROM THE WATER METER BOX (IN FRONT OF C
  3
USTOMER HOME).\P4)^ILP FORCE MAIN DROP CONNECTION AT MH SHALL INCLUDE A 2" GATE VALVE AND BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH JEA STANDARD PLATE NO. S-18. PROVIDE PROTECTIVE LINER TO RECEIVING MH (SEE SPEC #446). FOR OTHER LOCATION LIMITATIONS SEE DETAIL (W-10 & W-
  3
11).\P5)^IALL PS, PIPES (W/ LOCATE WIRES), VALVES AND FITTINGS WHICH ARE MAINTAINED BY JEA SHALL BE OF JEA APPROVED MATERIALS AND SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH JEA W&S STANDARD DETAILS.\P6)^IAS-BUILTS FOR THE UTILITIES WITHIN THE R/W SHALL BE
  3
 PROVIDED TO JEA IN ACCORDANCE WITH JEA STANDARDS. \P7)^IEACH RESIDENT MUST BE PRE APPROVED BY JEA'S ALTERNATIVE SEWER COMMITTEE TO BE ALLOWED TO CONNECT TO THE LP FORCE MAIN.\P8)^IEACH LOT/HOME MUST BE SERVED BY A SINGLE SERVICE CONNECTION (TANK, PUMP
  3
, SERVICE LINE, ELECTRICAL).\P9)^IEACH RESIDENT SHALL MAKE EVERY ATTEMPT TO LOCATE THE LP SYSTEM TANK BETWEEN THE HOUSE AND PUBLIC R/W AND SHALL BE EQUIPPED WITH AUDIBLE AND VISUAL ALARM CLEARLY VISIBLE FROM THE STREET.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\PALL WORK PERFORME
  3
D IN ACCORDANCE WITH LATEST JEA AND COJ STANDARD SPECIFICATIONS AND ALL APPLICABLE LOCAL AND STATE REGULATIONS (FDEP & COJ EPB RULE 3).\P\PPRESSURE AND LEAKAGE TESTING WILL BE PERFORMED IN ACCORDANCE WITH AWWA C600-87 OR OTHER APPLICABLE STANDARD.\P\
  3
PIN THE CASE WHERE SOLVENT CONTAMINATION IS FOUND IN THE TRENCH, WORK SHALL BE STOPPED AND PRIOR AUTHORITIES NOTIFIED. WORK MAY ONLY BE RESUMED WITH THE APPROVAL OF JEA AND FDEP.\P\PALL AIR RELEASE VALVES WILL BE PLACED AND CONSTRUCTED IN ACCORDANCE 
  1
WITH JEA STANDARDS.
