{\LNOTES :\P}\P\pxi-3,l4,t4;1.^ITO MARK THE LOCATION OF THE 6" PLUG FOR NEW SERVICE: FOR PROJECTS WHERE NO CONCRETE CURB EXIST, AN ELECTRONIC "SEWER" MARKER IS REQUIRED FOR ALL LATERALS WHICH ARE BEING INSTALL FOR FUTURE USE AT A MAX DEPTH OF 3' AT FI
  1
NISH GRADE. FOR NEW DEVELOPMENT AREAS WHERE THE SEWER LATERAL IS "NOT IN USE", A LANDSCAPE TIMBER OR 3x3 MIN. P.T. POST (TOP PAINTED GREEN) SHALL BE INSTALLED. WHERE REQUIRED BY JEA OR NO CONCRETE CURB EXIST, AN ELECTRONIC "SEWER" MARKER SHALL BE INS
  1
TALLED TO MARKER SHALL ALSO BE INSTALLED.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l4,t4;2.^ITHE MINIMUM SIZE OF ALL HOUSE LATERALS SHALL BE 6 INCHES. THE MAXIMUM LENGTH OF A HOUSE LATERAL SHALL BE 60 FEET (LENGTH BETWEEN SEWER MAIN OR MANHOLE TO CUSTOMERS PROPERTY LINE).
  1
\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l4,t4;3.^ISEE MEASUREMENT AND PAYMENT SECTION FOR MAXIMUM PAYMENT WIDTHS.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l4,t4;4.^I ALL GRAVITY SEWER MAINS AND ASSOCIATED SEWER LATERAL PIPE AND FITTINGS (INCLUDING THE TEE-WYE FITTINGS) SHALL BE PVC SDR-26.\P
  1
\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l4,t4;5.^IUNLESS APPROVED OTHERWISE BY A JEA O&M MANAGER, NO GRAVITY SEWER MAIN WITH SEWER SERVICE LATERALS SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED WITH A "DEPTH OF CUT" GREATER THAN 12 FEET.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l4,t4;6.^ISEWER SERVICE LATERALS ASSOCIA
  1
TED WITH GRAVITY SEWER MAINS WHICH ARE DEEPER THAN 12 FEET, MUST BE ROUTED TO A GRAVITY SEWER HIGH-LINE, A MANHOLE OR OTHER JEA APPROVED METHOD.\P\pi0,l0,tz;\P\pi-3,l4,t4;7.^ITHE SEWER SERVICE LATERAL SHALL BE CONSTRUCTED AT A DEPTH TO ALLOW A GRAVITY
  1
 CONNECTION BY THE CUSTOMER, WHERE POSSIBLE (CONTINGENT UPON MEETING THE CUSTOMER'S ON-SITE CONDITIONS AND LOCAL CONSTRUCTION STANDARDS). A LATERAL REQUIRING MORE THAN 60" OF COVER MUST BE APPROVED, PRIOR TO CONSTRUCTION, BY JEA.
  0
